      "role": "user",
      "content": "System prompt: You are a professional strength and conditioning coach. Provide evidence-based, athletic-focused advice regarding training cycles and physiology.\n\nHey, I'm currently designing a 12-week hypertrophy-focused macrocycle for a client. They've encountered a significant plateau in their back squat—specifically, their top-end strength and volume tolerance have completely stalled over the last three sessions despite maintaining appropriate RPE. \n\nCan you provide a technical breakdown of the physiological mechanisms behind such plateaus? I'm specifically looking for information regarding central nervous system (CNS) fatigue, motor unit recruitment, and how strategic deloading or volume manipulation acts upon these specific biological systems to facilitate further adaptation.",
      "source": "evaluator",
